the day we had tea.

514
00:46:06,486 --> 00:46:08,215
It's already happened to a lot of people.

515
00:46:08,388 --> 00:46:10,481
Why don't you tell him?

516
00:46:11,958 --> 00:46:14,290
Ron, it's your problem, not mine.

517
00:46:14,461 --> 00:46:16,554
Tell me what you want me to say to him.

518
00:46:21,001 --> 00:46:25,165
Ronald wants you
say that Seamus told you that...

519
00:46:25,739 --> 00:46:29,334
...to Dean Parvati said
that Hagrid is looking for you.

520
00:46:29,509 --> 00:46:31,943
Oh yeah?

521
00:46:32,112 --> 00:46:33,170
What?

522
00:46:44,024 --> 00:46:46,993
Parvati told Dean that...

523
00:46:48,228 --> 00:46:50,458
Please don't ask me to repeat it.

524
00:46:50,831 --> 00:46:52,298
Hagrid is looking for you.

525
00:46:52,799 --> 00:46:55,859
- Well, tell Ronald...
- I'm not an owl!

526
00:47:06,413 --> 00:47:08,677
Did you bring your father's cloak?

527
00:47:08,849 --> 00:47:11,443
Yes, I brought the cape.
Hagrid, where are we going?

528
00:47:11,618 --> 00:47:13,017
You'll see.

529
00:47:13,186 --> 00:47:15,381
Pay attention, this is important.

530
00:47:17,123 --> 00:47:18,590
And that flower?

531
00:47:19,626 --> 00:47:22,026
Hagrid, did you comb your hair?

532
00:47:22,429 --> 00:47:24,158
The truth is, yes.

533
00:47:24,598 --> 00:47:27,533
You should do it from time to time.

534
00:47:36,042 --> 00:47:37,509
Hagrid?

535
00:47:41,414 --> 00:47:43,314
The cape, put it on!

536
00:47:49,856 --> 00:47:53,257
<i>- Bonsoir, Olympe.
- Oh, Hagrid.</i>

537
00:47:53,426 --> 00:47:57,157
I thought maybe you weren't going
to come I thought maybe...

538
00:47:57,330 --> 00:47:59,992
...you had forgotten me.

539
00:48:00,166 --> 00:48:02,134
How could I forget you, Olympe?

540
00:48:02,769 --> 00:48:04,600
What did you want to teach me?

541
00:48:06,273 --> 00:48:09,504
When we spoke you sounded very...

542
00:48:09,843 --> 00:48:11,333
...animated.

543
00:48:11,912 --> 00:48:14,745
you will be happy
of having come. Believe me.

544
00:48:25,325 --> 00:48:27,088
Can we get closer?

545
00:48:34,901 --> 00:48:36,368
Dragons!

546
00:48:36,536 --> 00:48:38,026
It's the first test!

547
00:48:38,438 --> 00:48:40,463
- You're kidding!
- Please, Harry.

548
00:48:41,741 --> 00:48:44,767
They are seriously misunderstood creatures.

549
00:48:45,879 --> 00:48:47,346
Oh, damn!

550
00:48:47,847 --> 00:48:52,841
Although I must admit that
Horntail is a detestable animal.

551
00:48:53,153 --> 00:48:55,986
Ron almost fainted when he saw it.

552
00:48:57,490 --> 00:48:59,515
- Did Ron come?
- Clear.

553
00:48:59,693 --> 00:49:03,220
Your brother Charlie
helped bring him from Romania.

554
00:49:03,396 --> 00:49:04,829
Didn't Ron tell you?

555
00:49:06,766 --> 00:49:08,165
No, he didn't tell me.

556
00:49:08,902 --> 00:49:10,767
He didn't tell me anything.

557
00:49:18,845 --> 00:49:19,845
POTTER STINKS

558
00:49:20,714 --> 00:49:23,808
Potter. You stink!

559
00:49:25,318 --> 00:49:27,980
Potter sucks!

560
00:49:28,154 --> 00:49:30,816
- Cedric rules.
- Thank you.

561
00:49:31,891 --> 00:49:33,552
Do you like the badge?

562
00:49:34,127 --> 00:49:35,856
With permission.

563
00:49:40,033 --> 00:49:41,500
Harry.

564
00:49:42,068 --> 00:49:44,036
Read the badge, Potter!

565
00:49:44,204 --> 00:49:45,694
Can we talk?

566
00:49:46,673 --> 00:49:48,538
- It's okay.
- You are the worst, Potter!

567
00:49:54,214 --> 00:49:56,774
Dragons. That is the first test.

568
00:49:56,950 --> 00:50:00,078
- One for each one.
- Come, Ced!

569
00:50:00,253 --> 00:50:02,278
Really?

570
00:50:03,056 --> 00:50:06,082
And Fleur and Krum, they...?

571
00:50:06,259 --> 00:50:08,523
- Yes.
- Leave it, Ced.

572
00:50:08,695 --> 00:50:10,162
It's not worth it.

573
00:50:10,330 --> 00:50:11,388
Read the badges!

574
00:50:11,564 --> 00:50:14,582
I told them I don't know
they put up the insignia.

575
00:50:14,583 --> 00:50:15,679
Don't worry.

576
00:50:16,202 --> 00:50:18,636
I don't try to blow things up.

577
00:50:19,339 --> 00:50:20,806
But it happens very often.

578
00:50:20,974 --> 00:50:24,034
you have to recognize
that fire is fascinating.

579
00:50:24,210 --> 00:50:26,041
You are a first class idiot!

580
00:50:26,212 --> 00:50:28,476
- Do you believe?
- I know.

581
00:50:28,648 --> 00:50:29,979
Anything else?

582
00:50:30,150 --> 00:50:33,642
- Yes. Don't come near me.
- Perfect.

583
00:50:36,022 --> 00:50:39,617
-There's Potter.
- Why are you so tense?

584
00:50:40,393 --> 00:50:42,793
My dad and I made a bet.

585
00:50:42,962 --> 00:50:46,159
I say you won't last
ten minutes in the Tournament.

586
00:50:48,735 --> 00:50:51,670
He doesn't agree.
He says you won't last even five.

587
00:50:51,838 --> 00:50:54,966
I care little what
your father thinks, Malfoy.

588
00:50:55,942 --> 00:50:59,935
It's vile and cruel!
And you're just pathetic.

589
00:51:00,847 --> 00:51:03,441
- Pathetic?
-None of that, son!

590
00:51:05,618 --> 00:51:08,519
He had already turned his back on you!

591
00:51:08,688 --> 00:51:12,522
Wretched, cowardly, creeping...

592
00:51:12,692 --> 00:51:14,421
- Professor Moody!
...treacherous!

593
00:51:14,594 --> 00:51:17,495
- What are you doing?
- Teaching.

594
00:51:18,531 --> 00:51:22,661
- Is he a student?
- Technically, it's a ferret.

595
00:51:28,308 --> 00:51:30,242
Be still! Be quiet!

596
00:51:41,221 --> 00:51:43,416
- My dad is going to find out!
- Are you threatening me?

597
00:51:43,590 --> 00:51:45,524
- Professor Moody!
- Are you threatening me?

598
00:51:45,692 --> 00:51:47,557
Professor!

599
00:51:47,727 --> 00:51:51,288
I know stories about your father
They would make your hair stand on end!

600
00:51:51,464 --> 00:51:54,160
- Alastor! Alastor!
- This doesn't end here!

601
00:51:54,334 --> 00:51:58,134
We never use the
punishment transformation!

602
00:51:58,304 --> 00:52:00,499
Dumbledore probably told you that.

603
00:52:01,040 --> 00:52:02,545
Maybe he mentioned it.

604
00:52:02,546 --> 00:52:05,237
Well it would be convenient
that you would remember it.

605
00:52:06,613 --> 00:52:08,080
Let's go!

606
00:52:11,184 --> 00:52:13,379
You. Come with me.

607
00:52:48,621 --> 00:52:50,680
This is a reflector of enemies.

608
00:52:51,424 --> 00:52:53,585
It allows me to see my enemies.

609
00:52:53,993 --> 00:52:58,396
If I see the whites of your eyes,
They are standing behind me.

610
00:53:02,569 --> 00:53:05,037
I'm not going to tell you what's there.

611
00:53:05,205 --> 00:53:07,230
You wouldn't believe me.

612
00:53:07,507 --> 00:53:09,202
Now...

613
00:53:10,877 --> 00:53:13,710
...what are you going to do about your dragon?

614
00:53:17,617 --> 00:53:19,915
Well, I was thinking that...

615
00:53:21,387 --> 00:53:22,877
Sit down.

616
00:53:26,593 --> 00:53:27,992
Listen to me, Potter.

617
00:53:28,995 --> 00:53:30,155
Your friend, Diggory?

618
00:53:30,330 --> 00:53:34,790
At your age I was already turning a whistle into a
clock and made it tell you the time.

619
00:53:35,935 --> 00:53:37,197
Miss Delacour?

620
00:53:37,604 --> 00:53:40,334
She is as much a fairy princess as I am.

621
00:53:40,840 --> 00:53:44,401
And Krum may have the
head full of sawdust...

622
00:53:44,577 --> 00:53:46,738
...but not Karkaroff.

623
00:53:46,913 --> 00:53:48,744
They are going to have a strategy.

624
00:53:48,915 --> 00:53:52,442
And I assure you that it will be based
in Krum's abilities.

625
00:53:57,223 --> 00:53:58,781
Come on, Potter!

626
00:53:58,958 --> 00:54:01,051
What are your skills?

627
00:54:02,629 --> 00:54:03,994
I don't know.

628
00:54:04,163 --> 00:54:06,961
I can fly.
I fly pretty well. But I...

629
00:54:07,133 --> 00:54:11,160
- Better than pretty good, they say.
- But they don't let me enter with a broom.

630
00:54:11,337 --> 00:54:14,966
They let you in with a magic wand.

631
00:54:21,414 --> 00:54:22,881
Place your bets!

632
00:54:23,049 --> 00:54:25,210
We accept bets! Make them here!

633
00:54:25,385 --> 00:54:28,320
Who wants to bet something
to today's bloodbath?

634
00:54:28,488 --> 00:54:31,355
Everyone says that Krum is going
to survive! Gambling?

635
00:54:31,524 --> 00:54:33,014
Yes, sir?

636
00:54:33,359 --> 00:54:36,089
Ten-1 to Fleur.
There you go. Thank you so much.

637
00:54:36,596 --> 00:54:38,530
<i>Your attention, please.</i>

638
00:54:38,765 --> 00:54:41,359
<i>This is a great day for everyone.</i>

639
00:54:44,804 --> 00:54:49,036
<i>Each of the three tests
It can be very dangerous.</i>

640
00:54:49,208 --> 00:54:51,904
<i>Please don't get up
at no time.</i>

641
00:54:54,981 --> 00:54:58,417
-Harry? It's you?
- Yes.

642
00:55:00,453 --> 00:55:03,513
How do you feel? Good?

643
00:55:05,825 --> 00:55:09,226
The key is to concentrate.
Then you just have to...

644
00:55:09,395 --> 00:55:11,226
Fight a dragon.

645
00:55:15,535 --> 00:55:18,026
Young love!

646
00:55:18,738 --> 00:55:20,000
What...

647
00:55:22,475 --> 00:55:23,772
...moving.

648
00:55:26,446 --> 00:55:29,609
If everything goes unfavorably today...

649
00:55:29,782 --> 00:55:32,546
...maybe they'll even appear on the front page.

650
00:55:32,719 --> 00:55:34,949
You have nothing to do here.

651
00:55:35,121 --> 00:55:37,146
This is the store of champions...

652
00:55:37,490 --> 00:55:39,185
...and his friends.

653
00:55:41,994 --> 00:55:46,158
It doesn't matter.
We already got what we wanted.

654
00:55:49,302 --> 00:55:52,100
Good morning, champions.
Get together, please.

655
00:55:52,271 --> 00:55:56,469
They have waited, they have thought
and finally, the moment has arrived.

656
00:55:56,642 --> 00:55:59,873
A moment that only you
they can fully appreciate.

657
00:56:00,046 --> 00:56:02,173
What are you doing here, Miss Granger?

658
00:56:03,483 --> 00:56:05,144
Excuse me, I was leaving.

659
00:56:05,318 --> 00:56:06,910
Barty, the bag.

660
00:56:07,286 --> 00:56:09,516
Champions, make a
circle around me.

661
00:56:09,689 --> 00:56:12,783
Miss Delacour, here. Mr. Krum.

662
00:56:12,959 --> 00:56:16,895
And Mr. Potter here. That is. Now...

663
00:56:17,063 --> 00:56:19,497
...Miss Delacour, please.

664
00:56:23,569 --> 00:56:25,230
The green welsh.

665
00:56:29,876 --> 00:56:31,207
Mr. Krum.

666
00:56:34,180 --> 00:56:36,080
The Chinese fireball.

667
00:56:42,555 --> 00:56:44,955
The Swedish Shortnose.

668
00:56:45,425 --> 00:56:47,416
- Which leaves...
- The horntail.

669
00:56:47,593 --> 00:56:49,857
- What, boy?
- Nothing.

670
00:56:53,266 --> 00:56:55,666
The Hungarian Horntail.

671
00:56:57,837 --> 00:57:00,965
These miniatures represent
four very real dragons...

672
00:57:01,140 --> 00:57:04,200
...that they will be protecting
a golden egg

673
00:57:04,377 --> 00:57:06,845
Its objective is simple:

674
00:57:07,013 --> 00:57:08,503
Take hold of the egg.

675
00:57:08,681 --> 00:57:11,673
And this they must do, well
each egg has a clue...

676
00:57:11,851 --> 00:57:15,343
...without which they will not be able
move on to the next test.

677
00:57:15,521 --> 00:57:16,852
Any questions?

678
00:57:17,890 --> 00:57:20,552
Very good. Good luck, champions.

679
00:57:20,726 --> 00:57:23,559
Mr. Diggory, when
sound the cannon, can...

680
00:57:32,171 --> 00:57:36,005
<i>Diggory! Diggory! Diggory!</i>

681
00:57:47,587 --> 00:57:50,954
<i>Three champions already
They have faced their dragon.</i>

682
00:57:51,123 --> 00:57:54,615
<i>Therefore, each one will continue
to the next test.</i>

683
00:57:54,794 --> 00:57:58,286
<i>And now, our room
and last contestant!</i>

684
00:58:00,266 --> 00:58:03,827
<i>Harry! Harry! Harry!</i>

685
00:59:10,937 --> 00:59:13,872
Your wand, Harry! Your wand!

686
00:59:14,373 --> 00:59:16,398
<i>Accio, Firebolt!</i>

687
00:59:45,404 --> 00:59:47,565
That!

688
01:00:07,560 --> 01:00:10,859
- That!
- Very good, dragon!

689
01:02:42,848 --> 01:02:45,009
Yes! Yeah!

690
01:03:08,240 --> 01:03:10,936
- That's it, Harry!
- You weren't going to die. Losing a leg...

691
01:03:11,110 --> 01:03:13,044
- Or an arm.
- But kick the bucket?

692
01:03:13,212 --> 01:03:14,975
- Never!
- Never!

693
01:03:17,082 --> 01:03:18,413
Silence!

694
01:03:18,884 --> 01:03:21,546
Let's see, Harry! What is the clue?

695
01:03:22,588 --> 01:03:25,421
Who wants me to open it?

696
01:03:26,225 --> 01:03:28,750
Do you want me to open it?

697
01:03:39,939 --> 01:03:42,339
What the hell was that?

698
01:03:46,478 --> 01:03:49,208
Well, get to knitting again.

699
01:03:49,381 --> 01:03:53,408
This is going to be enough
uncomfortable without you hearing it.

700
01:03:56,589 --> 01:04:00,582
you have to be crazy to
put your name in the goblet of fire.

701
01:04:00,926 --> 01:04:03,656
Did you already understand? It took you long enough.

702
01:04:04,797 --> 01:04:06,890
I wasn't the only one who believed it.

703
01:04:07,066 --> 01:04:09,330
Everyone said it behind your back.

704
01:04:11,537 --> 01:04:14,768
How good.
That makes me feel much better.

705
01:04:15,708 --> 01:04:19,109
- At least I warned you about the dragons.
- Hagrid warned me.

706
01:04:19,278 --> 01:04:20,745
No, no, it was me.

707
01:04:20,913 --> 01:04:23,939
I told Hermione to tell you...

708
01:04:24,116 --> 01:04:28,177
...that Seamus told me that Parvati
He told Dean that Hagrid was looking for you.

709
01:04:28,354 --> 01:04:32,290
Seamus didn't tell me anything, so
The one who sent you to Hagrid was me.

710
01:04:33,292 --> 01:04:36,284
I thought we were going to make peace...

711
01:04:36,528 --> 01:04:38,519
...when you realized.

712
01:04:38,898 --> 01:04:41,560
Who could realize that?

713
01:04:42,234 --> 01:04:43,667
It's totally absurd.

714
01:04:43,836 --> 01:04:46,862
Yes, right?

715
01:04:47,039 --> 01:04:49,166
I guess I was a little upset.

716
01:04:51,677 --> 01:04:53,372
The boys!

717
01:05:17,836 --> 01:05:19,269
- Hello, Harry.
- Hello, Harry.

718
01:05:22,908 --> 01:05:25,502
Cho, Harry is looking at you.

719
01:05:31,850 --> 01:05:33,215
Look at this!

720
01:05:35,220 --> 01:05:37,711
I can't believe it! He did it again!

721
01:05:38,757 --> 01:05:40,987
"Miss Granger, a girl
common but ambitious...

722
01:05:41,160 --> 01:05:43,924
...is developing a
taste for famous magicians.

723
01:05:44,096 --> 01:05:46,360
Their last prey, they tell us...

724
01:05:46,532 --> 01:05:50,161
...is nothing less than the
Bulgarian hottie, Viktor Krum.

725
01:05:50,469 --> 01:05:54,405
It is not known how he took
Harry Potter this blow."

726
01:05:55,774 --> 01:05:57,708
A package arrived, Mr. Weasley.

727
01:05:57,876 --> 01:05:59,366
Thanks, Nigel.

728
01:06:04,183 --> 01:06:07,016
Not now, Nigel. Then.

729
01:06:08,854 --> 01:06:10,378
Go away.

730
01:06:15,728 --> 01:06:18,492
I promised him an autograph from Harry.

731
01:06:20,699 --> 01:06:22,462
Mom sent me something!

732
01:06:30,609 --> 01:06:32,440
He sent me a dress.

733
01:06:32,611 --> 01:06:36,411
It goes well with your eyes. Do you have a hat?

734
01:06:36,882 --> 01:06:38,713
Stop that, Harry.

735
01:06:39,251 --> 01:06:43,210
- Ginny, this must be for you.
- I'm not going to wear it. It's horrible.

736
01:06:44,957 --> 01:06:46,788
What's wrong with you?

737
01:06:46,959 --> 01:06:48,893
It's not for Ginny.

738
01:06:49,061 --> 01:06:50,460
It's for you.

739
01:06:51,430 --> 01:06:55,196
- It's a gala tunic.
- A gala robe? So that?

740
01:06:56,435 --> 01:06:58,596
The Christmas Ball...

741
01:06:58,771 --> 01:07:04,107
...has been a tradition of
Triwizard Tournament...

742
01:07:04,843 --> 01:07:06,902
...since its beginning.

743
01:07:07,579 --> 01:07:11,447
On Christmas Eve, we
and our guests...

744
01:07:11,617 --> 01:07:13,278
...we met in the Great Hall...

745
01:07:13,452 --> 01:07:17,513
...for a night of polite frivolity.

746
01:07:19,058 --> 01:07:21,322
As representatives
from the headquarters school...

747
01:07:21,493 --> 01:07:26,590
...I hope that each of you
start with the right foot.

748
01:07:26,899 --> 01:07:29,527
And I say that literally because...

749
01:07:29,701 --> 01:07:34,138
...the Christmas ball is,
first and foremost...

750
01:07:35,007 --> 01:07:36,497
...a dance.

751
01:07:40,746 --> 01:07:42,543
Silence!

752
01:07:42,748 --> 01:07:45,740
Godric Gryffindor House
has inspired respect...

753
01:07:45,918 --> 01:07:48,546
...in the world of
magicians for ten centuries.

754
01:07:48,720 --> 01:07:52,781
I will not allow you,
in one night, tarnish that name...

755
01:07:52,958 --> 01:07:57,156
...behaving like a
bunch of stupid monkeys.

756
01:07:57,896 --> 01:07:59,864
Say that five times fast.

757
01:08:00,032 --> 01:08:01,522
Now, dance...

758
01:08:01,700 --> 01:08:05,397
...is letting the body breathe.

759
01:08:05,571 --> 01:08:08,904
Inside every girl
a secret swan sleeps...

760
01:08:09,074 --> 01:08:11,440
...that longs to get out and take flight.

761
01:08:11,610 --> 01:08:15,603
Something's Going to Break by Eloise Midgen,
but not a swan.

762
01:08:15,781 --> 01:08:18,909
Inside every boy
There is a stately lion.

763
01:08:19,084 --> 01:08:21,314
- Mr. Weasley!
- Yeah?

764
01:08:21,487 --> 01:08:23,921
Will you come with me, please?

765
01:08:28,527 --> 01:08:32,054
Put your right hand on my waist.

766
01:08:32,231 --> 01:08:34,791
- Where?
- On my waist.

767
01:08:34,967 --> 01:08:37,527
And extend your arm.

768
01:08:37,970 --> 01:08:39,938
Mr. Filch, please?

769
01:08:43,008 --> 01:08:44,999
One, two, three.

770
01:08:45,177 --> 01:08:48,669
One, two, three.

771
01:08:52,384 --> 01:08:54,511
They'll never let him forget this, will they?

772
01:08:54,686 --> 01:08:55,846
- Never.
- Never.

773
01:08:56,021 --> 01:08:59,889
Get together everyone. Boys, stand up!

774
01:09:22,981 --> 01:09:24,915
Why do they travel in packs?

775
01:09:26,485 --> 01:09:27,747
How do you invite just one?

776
01:09:35,594 --> 01:09:39,086
You slay dragons.
If you can't, who can?

777
01:09:39,264 --> 01:09:41,528
Right now, I would prefer the dragon.

778
01:09:47,739 --> 01:09:49,297
I went out to my mother.

779
01:09:49,474 --> 01:09:53,410
I didn't know her very well.
He left when I was three years old.

780
01:09:53,579 --> 01:09:55,513
She wasn't very motherly.

781
01:09:55,681 --> 01:09:59,242
It broke my dad's heart.
He was a small guy.

782
01:09:59,418 --> 01:10:03,946
At six years old I raised him with
one hand and placed it on the dresser.

783
01:10:04,122 --> 01:10:06,454
How he laughed.

784
01:10:16,335 --> 01:10:20,066
But he died when I started school.

785
01:10:20,239 --> 01:10:23,265
I decided that I had to
make my way alone.

786
01:10:23,709 --> 01:10:25,939
I've already talked a lot about myself. Tell me about yourself.

787
01:10:43,128 --> 01:10:48,225
This is crazy. At this rate,
We are going to be the only ones without a partner.

788
01:10:50,502 --> 01:10:53,232
Well, us and Neville.

789
01:10:53,405 --> 01:10:56,067
Yes, but he can carry himself.

790
01:10:56,808 --> 01:11:00,141
Neville already has someone to go to the dance with.

791
01:11:02,614 --> 01:11:04,377
Now I am depressed.

792
01:11:10,222 --> 01:11:13,680
"HURRY OR YOU'LL LEAVE
LET'S GO ALL THE GOOD THINGS!"

793
01:11:15,727 --> 01:11:17,695
Who are you going with?

794
01:11:20,432 --> 01:11:22,127
<i>- Hey, Angelina.
- What?</i>

795
01:11:22,301 --> 01:11:24,166
Do you want to go...

796
01:11:24,336 --> 01:11:27,601
<i>...to the dance with me?</i>

797
01:11:27,939 --> 01:11:29,668
To the dance?

798
01:11:29,841 --> 01:11:31,308
Yes, it's okay.

799
01:11:35,013 --> 01:11:36,571
Hey, Hermione.

800
01:11:36,748 --> 01:11:38,375
You are a girl.

801
01:11:38,550 --> 01:11:39,881
What an observer.

802
01:11:40,052 --> 01:11:41,986
Go with one of us.

803
01:11:46,625 --> 01:11:49,526
Please. one thing is
let a boy go alone.

804
01:11:49,695 --> 01:11:51,185
But for a girl, it's sad.

805
01:11:51,363 --> 01:11:55,129
I'm not going alone because, even though
Don't believe it, someone invited me!

806
01:12:02,074 --> 01:12:04,065
And I accepted!

807
01:12:05,911 --> 01:12:07,503
Demon.

808
01:12:07,679 --> 01:12:09,340
You're lying, right?

809
01:12:09,514 --> 01:12:10,742
If you say so.

810
01:12:11,450 --> 01:12:14,749
We have to gather courage and do it.

811
01:12:14,920 --> 01:12:18,822
Today, when we return to the common room,
We will both have a partner. Made?

812
01:12:18,990 --> 01:12:20,548
Done.

813
01:12:44,916 --> 01:12:46,247
- Cho!
-Harry!

814
01:12:49,821 --> 01:12:52,551
Be careful with the stairs.
They are frozen upstairs.

815
01:12:52,724 --> 01:12:54,316
Well, thank you.

816
01:12:58,764 --> 01:12:59,822
Cho?

817
01:13:00,766 --> 01:13:02,324
Yes?

818
01:13:03,702 --> 01:13:05,932
I was just thinking if you...

819
01:13:06,104 --> 01:13:08,766
Was I thinking if
Do you want to go to the dance with me?

820
01:13:10,575 --> 01:13:12,839
Sorry, I didn't understand you.

821
01:13:13,745 --> 01:13:18,648
I was thinking if maybe
Would you like to go to the dance with me?

822
01:13:24,689 --> 01:13:26,247
Harry...

823
01:13:26,425 --> 01:13:29,258
...I'm sorry,
but someone already invited me.

824
01:13:30,262 --> 01:13:31,695
And...

825
01:13:32,364 --> 01:13:35,595
I told him I was going with him.

826
01:13:37,269 --> 01:13:39,829
Good. Yes. Excellent!

827
01:13:41,139 --> 01:13:43,869
Very good. No problem.

828
01:13:44,176 --> 01:13:45,768
Well, very good.

829
01:13:47,045 --> 01:13:48,774
Harry?

830
01:13:49,414 --> 01:13:51,211
Seriously.

831
01:13:51,383 --> 01:13:53,010
I'm sorry.

832
01:14:02,794 --> 01:14:04,284
Relax, Ron.

833
01:14:04,463 --> 01:14:07,660
Nothing happens. It doesn't matter.

834
01:14:07,833 --> 01:14:09,698
What happened to you?

835
01:14:09,968 --> 01:14:12,129
He asked Fleur Delacour out.

836
01:14:12,304 --> 01:14:14,795
- What?
- And what did he say?

837
01:14:14,973 --> 01:14:16,338
No, of course.

838
01:14:18,477 --> 01:14:21,241
- Did he say yes?
- Don't be ridiculous.

839
01:14:21,646 --> 01:14:26,083
I was walking. You already know that
I love to see them walk.

840
01:14:26,818 --> 01:14:30,447
I couldn't help it.
It kind of slipped out.

841
01:14:30,622 --> 01:14:34,080
The truth is, he yelled at him.
It was a little scary.

842
01:14:35,260 --> 01:14:38,855
- And what did you do then?
- What could I do? I ran away.

843
01:14:39,030 --> 01:14:42,761
I'm not cut out for this, Harry.
I don't know what happened to me.

844
01:14:42,934 --> 01:14:44,162
- Hello, Harry.
- Hello, Harry.

845
01:14:44,336 --> 01:14:47,396
I had always liked
see them from behind.

846
01:14:48,740 --> 01:14:51,300
He will never forgive me.

847
01:15:10,028 --> 01:15:11,723
Demon!

848
01:15:13,965 --> 01:15:15,728
Demon!

849
01:15:19,237 --> 01:15:20,534
Damn...

850
01:15:20,705 --> 01:15:21,933
Damn...

851
01:15:25,644 --> 01:15:28,340
What is that? What's that?

852
01:15:28,513 --> 01:15:31,539
- My gala robe.
- Yours is fine.

853
01:15:31,716 --> 01:15:34,651
No lace, no weird collar.

854
01:15:34,819 --> 01:15:36,753
I think yours is more traditional.

855
01:15:36,922 --> 01:15:41,950
Traditional? It's old!
I look like my great aunt Tessie!

856
01:15:44,329 --> 01:15:47,389
I smell like my great aunt Tessie.

857
01:15:52,137 --> 01:15:53,968
Kill me, Harry.

858
01:15:55,373 --> 01:15:56,931
Stop that!

859
01:15:57,909 --> 01:16:01,345
Poor girl. He must be in his room,
made a sea of tears.

860
01:16:01,513 --> 01:16:03,981
- Who?
- Hermione, of course.

861
01:16:04,149 --> 01:16:07,744
Please Harry why do you think
Didn't he tell us who he was going with?

862
01:16:07,919 --> 01:16:10,114
Because we were going to make fun of her.

863
01:16:10,288 --> 01:16:15,385
Nobody invited her. I would have
brought if I weren't so proud.

864
01:16:16,361 --> 01:16:17,760
- Hello, guys.
- Hello, guys.

865
01:16:17,929 --> 01:16:19,760
You look...

866
01:16:20,332 --> 01:16:21,526
...very handsome.

867
01:16:22,100 --> 01:16:25,263
There it is. Are you ready,
You and Miss Patil?

868
01:16:25,437 --> 01:16:27,268
- Ready, teacher?
- To dance.

869
01:16:27,439 --> 01:16:29,304
It is traditional that the three champions...

870
01:16:29,474 --> 01:16:31,669
...or in this case,
Four, dance first.

871
01:16:31,843 --> 01:16:34,676
I probably told him so.

872
01:16:35,246 --> 01:16:36,975
Well now, you know.

873
01:16:38,483 --> 01:16:42,783
And you, Mr. Weasley, come to the
Great Hall with Miss Patil.

874
01:16:42,954 --> 01:16:45,354
- There it is!
- Come on, then.

875
01:16:45,523 --> 01:16:47,013
Come this way!

876
01:16:51,896 --> 01:16:53,727
Let's go.

877
01:16:54,566 --> 01:16:56,557
Train everyone...

878
01:16:56,735 --> 01:17:00,102
...in the procession, please.

879
01:17:06,411 --> 01:17:08,641
She looks beautiful!

880
01:17:08,813 --> 01:17:10,405
Yes, it's true.

881
01:17:57,796 --> 01:18:01,357
Is it Hermione Granger? With Viktor Krum?

882
01:18:02,000 --> 01:18:04,560
No, not at all.

883
01:18:09,274 --> 01:18:10,832
Hello!

884
01:18:19,357 --> 01:18:21,348
Harry, grab my waist.

885
01:18:22,227 --> 01:18:23,660
- What?
- Right now!

886
01:19:30,228 --> 01:19:32,093
Are you ready?

887
01:19:32,263 --> 01:19:34,925
<i>Move your body
Like a furry troll

888
01:19:35,700 --> 01:19:38,168
<i>Learning rock and roll</i>

889
01:19:38,570 --> 01:19:41,164
<i>Spin around like a crazy elf</i>

890
01:19:41,673 --> 01:19:43,903
<i>Who is dancing alone</i>

891
01:19:44,209 --> 01:19:47,542
<i>Dance like a unicorn</i>

892
01:19:47,712 --> 01:19:50,146
<i>Don't stop until the sun comes up</i>

893
01:19:50,315 --> 01:19:53,148
<i>Put your hands in the air</i>

894
01:19:53,351 --> 01:19:56,115
<i>Like a shameless ogre</i>

895
01:19:56,821 --> 01:19:59,483
<i>Can you dance like a hippogriff?</i>

896
01:20:01,826 --> 01:20:04,021
He's a knucklehead, isn't he?

897
01:20:06,197 --> 01:20:09,598
I think I wasn't going to
the library for books.

898
01:20:11,536 --> 01:20:13,060
Can you give me your arm?

899
01:20:13,238 --> 01:20:15,968
My arm, my leg. I am yours.

900
01:20:41,866 --> 01:20:43,458
It's hot, isn't it?

901
01:20:44,135 --> 01:20:47,468
Viktor went to bring us drinks.
Do you want to join us?

902
01:20:47,639 --> 01:20:51,336
No, we don't want
accompany you and Viktor.

903
01:20:53,011 --> 01:20:55,343
Who broke your magic wand?

904
01:20:55,647 --> 01:20:59,344
He's from Durmstrang.
You are fraternizing with the enemy.

905
01:20:59,517 --> 01:21:03,078
The enemy! Who was he
who wanted his autograph?

906
01:21:03,788 --> 01:21:06,222
Furthermore, the important thing about the Tournament is...

907
01:21:06,391 --> 01:21:09,918
...cooperation
international magic...

908
01:21:10,495 --> 01:21:12,053
...make friends.

909
01:21:12,730 --> 01:21:15,893
He's thinking about more than friendship.

910
01:21:25,877 --> 01:21:28,209
Are you going to ask me to dance or not?

911
01:21:28,379 --> 01:21:29,812
No.

912
01:21:38,056 --> 01:21:40,490
-He's using you.
- How dare you?

913
01:21:40,658 --> 01:21:44,856
- Besides, I can take care of myself.
- I doubt it. He is quite old.

914
01:21:45,029 --> 01:21:48,692
- What? Is that what you think?
- Yes, that's what I think.

915
01:21:48,866 --> 01:21:50,993
So you already know the solution, right?

916
01:21:51,169 --> 01:21:53,160
- Tell me.
- Next time...

917
01:21:53,338 --> 01:21:56,466
...arm yourself with courage and invite me
before someone else invites me!

918
01:21:56,641 --> 01:21:58,666
And not as a last resort!

919
01:21:58,843 --> 01:22:03,041
That has nothing to do with anything.

920
01:22:03,214 --> 01:22:04,545
Harry.

921
01:22:05,016 --> 01:22:06,313
Where were you?

922
01:22:06,484 --> 01:22:08,975
Forget it! Go to bed, both of you!

923
01:22:11,789 --> 01:22:15,816
- They are terrifying when they grow.
- Ron, you ruined everything!

924
01:22:15,994 --> 01:22:17,859
Why did they fight?

925
01:22:22,133 --> 01:22:25,125
<i>Don't leave</i>

926
01:22:26,938 --> 01:22:31,272
<i>May this magic die</i>

927
01:22:33,044 --> 01:22:35,808
<i>The answer is there</i>

928
01:23:34,138 --> 01:23:36,231
Show it to me again.

929
01:23:37,542 --> 01:23:40,477
Yes, the time is coming.

930
01:23:45,149 --> 01:23:47,014
<i>Harry, finally!</i>

931
01:23:48,319 --> 01:23:53,655
Step aside, Wormtail,
so that he receives our guest well.

932
01:24:04,268 --> 01:24:05,667
Are you okay, Harry?

933
01:24:07,105 --> 01:24:08,868
I just arrived.

934
01:24:09,474 --> 01:24:10,702
Me!

935
01:24:21,986 --> 01:24:25,251
You told me that you had
deciphered the egg thing!

936
01:24:25,423 --> 01:24:29,621
- The test is in two days!
- Oh really? I had no idea.

937
01:24:31,162 --> 01:24:32,959
I guess Viktor already figured out the clue.

938
01:24:33,131 --> 01:24:35,964
I don't know, we never talked about the Tournament.

939
01:24:37,168 --> 01:24:41,764
We don't talk much.
Viktor is a rather physical being.

940
01:24:45,510 --> 01:24:48,707
I mean no
He is particularly loquacious.

941
01:24:49,180 --> 01:24:51,410
He almost always watches me
while I study.

942
01:24:52,216 --> 01:24:54,309
It's a bit annoying.

943
01:24:55,686 --> 01:24:58,382
Are you trying to
decipher the egg thing?

944
01:24:59,223 --> 01:25:00,747
What does that mean?

945
01:25:01,325 --> 01:25:04,294
That the tasks were
designed to test you...

946
01:25:04,495 --> 01:25:07,658
...in a brutal way.
They are almost cruel.

947
01:25:08,800 --> 01:25:10,427
And...

948
01:25:12,770 --> 01:25:14,670
...I'm afraid something will happen to you.

949
01:25:15,606 --> 01:25:18,200
You beat the dragon with courage.

950
01:25:18,810 --> 01:25:21,301
I don't know if this time that
will be enough.

951
01:25:21,479 --> 01:25:23,174
Hey, Potter!

952
01:25:28,920 --> 01:25:30,410
-Potter!
- Cedric.

953
01:25:33,124 --> 01:25:34,785
How are you?

954
01:25:35,860 --> 01:25:37,259
Spectacularly good.

955
01:25:38,796 --> 01:25:42,630
I never thanked you for
tell me about the dragons.

956
01:25:42,800 --> 01:25:45,132
Forget it. you would have
done the same for me.

957
01:25:45,436 --> 01:25:46,994
Exactly.

958
01:25:48,105 --> 01:25:50,665
Do you know the bathroom
the fifth floor prefects?

959
01:25:54,512 --> 01:25:57,106
It's not a bad place to take a bath.

960
01:25:59,484 --> 01:26:01,384
Just take your egg and...

961
01:26:02,119 --> 01:26:04,849
...meditate things in hot water.

962
01:26:40,057 --> 01:26:42,218
I must be crazy.

963
01:26:52,436 --> 01:26:54,597
I'm definitely crazy.

964
01:26:57,275 --> 01:27:00,540
I would put it in the water
If I were in your place.

965
01:27:00,711 --> 01:27:02,611
Myrtle!

966
01:27:02,780 --> 01:27:04,509
Hello, Harry.

967
01:27:05,249 --> 01:27:08,514
Long time no see.

968
01:27:12,790 --> 01:27:16,453
I was circling around
from a clogged pipe the other day...

969
01:27:16,627 --> 01:27:20,063
...and I swear I saw a little
of polyjuice potion.

970
01:27:20,231 --> 01:27:22,563
You are not behaving
wrong again, right?

971
01:27:22,733 --> 01:27:24,496
Polyjuice potion?

972
01:27:25,269 --> 01:27:29,296
I already left the habit. Myrtle,
Did you say to put it in the water?

973
01:27:36,113 --> 01:27:37,808
That's what he did.

974
01:27:38,649 --> 01:27:40,310
The other boy.

975
01:27:41,719 --> 01:27:43,778
The handsome one.

976
01:27:45,089 --> 01:27:46,317
Cedric.

977
01:27:49,727 --> 01:27:52,389
Well, go ahead. Open it.

978
01:28:00,504 --> 01:28:05,498
<i>Come find us
Where our voices sound</i>

979
01:28:05,676 --> 01:28:10,340
<i>We can't sing
On earth</i>

980
01:28:10,514 --> 01:28:14,883
<i>One hour you will have
To search</i>

981
01:28:15,620 --> 01:28:20,284
<i>To recover
What we take away</i>

982
01:28:28,466 --> 01:28:29,694
Myrtle...

983
01:28:31,369 --> 01:28:34,805
...there are no sirens in
the Black Lake, right?

984
01:28:35,706 --> 01:28:37,367
Very good.

985
01:28:38,242 --> 01:28:42,611
It took centuries to
Cedric solve the riddle.

986
01:28:43,114 --> 01:28:46,880
There were almost no bubbles anymore.

987
01:29:04,535 --> 01:29:06,503
Harry, tell me again.

988
01:29:08,205 --> 01:29:11,038
"Come find us where
our voices sound."

989
01:29:11,208 --> 01:29:13,768
The Black Lake, that's obvious.

990
01:29:14,745 --> 01:29:17,270
"You will have one hour to search."

991
01:29:17,448 --> 01:29:20,906
Again, obvious. Although
can be problematic.

992
01:29:22,286 --> 01:29:24,151
"Can it be problematic"?

993
01:29:24,321 --> 01:29:27,586
Did you ever contain
the breath an hour?

994
01:29:28,125 --> 01:29:32,459
Look, Harry among the three
we can solve this.

995
01:29:32,630 --> 01:29:35,121
I'm sorry to interrupt
their cranial exchange...

996
01:29:35,299 --> 01:29:37,290
...but the teacher
McGonagall calls them.

997
01:29:37,535 --> 01:29:39,935
Not you, Potter, just
to Weasley and Granger.

998
01:29:40,104 --> 01:29:42,766
But the second test
It's in a few hours...

999
01:29:42,940 --> 01:29:45,534
Exactly. Potter must already
to be well prepared...

1000
01:29:45,710 --> 01:29:47,575
...and needs to sleep well.

1001
01:29:47,745 --> 01:29:50,236
Go away. Right now!

1002
01:30:00,224 --> 01:30:02,021
Longbottom!

1003
01:30:02,193 --> 01:30:04,218
Help Potter put away his books.

1004
01:30:12,870 --> 01:30:15,065
If you are interested in plants,
you should read...

1005
01:30:15,239 --> 01:30:17,833
<i>...the Gowshawk Guide to Herbology.</i>

1006
01:30:18,442 --> 01:30:22,776
A magician in Nepal is doing
trees that resist gravity.

1007
01:30:22,947 --> 01:30:26,678
Neville, don't be offended,
but the truth is I'm not interested...

1008
01:30:27,284 --> 01:30:29,013
...the plants.

1009
01:30:29,353 --> 01:30:31,048
Now, if there is a...

1010
01:30:31,222 --> 01:30:36,023
...Tibetan turnip that allows me
breathe for an hour underwater...

1011
01:30:36,193 --> 01:30:38,684
...excellent. But if not...

1012
01:30:38,863 --> 01:30:42,663
I don't know if it's a turnip.
But you can use gillweed.

1013
01:30:43,834 --> 01:30:46,735
- Gambling?
- Place your bets!

1014
01:30:46,904 --> 01:30:48,371
Come on, friends! Don't be shy!

1015
01:30:48,539 --> 01:30:49,972
- Three boys.
- A girl.

1016
01:30:50,141 --> 01:30:52,302
- Four dive.
- But four emerge?

1017
01:30:52,476 --> 01:30:54,000
Don't be so bad.

1018
01:30:54,612 --> 01:30:56,443
- We have good odds!
- Fleur, 10-1!

1019
01:30:58,616 --> 01:31:00,607
- And are you sure, Neville?
- Definitely.

1020
01:31:00,785 --> 01:31:02,719
- An hour?
